-- recordType — wrap a list of field-entry records into a `$record` FenelType
-- value: [FieldEntry] → {$record: {fields: …}}.
--
-- FM-retire-4 Step 1 (typed-function-references) — the general runtime
-- type-builder. There was no std primitive that authors a `$record` Type
-- VALUE from field data (only state:loadType/schemaOf, which LOAD an
-- already-registered type). The `forms` module open-coded it as
-- buildFormType's `assocRecord {} "$record" (assocRecord {} "fields" …)`
-- because Fenel record LITERALS can't carry a `$`-prefixed key (the lexer
-- starts idents at [\p{L}_]) — `std:assocRecord` builds the `$`-key envelope
-- dynamically. Extracted here so any dynamic-type surface (not just forms)
-- can construct a record type from field data.
--
-- FM-retire-10 (2026-06-07) — promoted from a bare-body extraction (loaded as
-- `std-recordType` purely for its body, with the params/returns/facets in a TS
-- `defineFunction`) to a full `module std where` bodied member. Its `-> Type`
-- return rides the Ext1 `Type` type-atom. std.ts drops the recordType spec +
-- the body-extraction seam.
--
-- Pure. `fields` is the projected field-entry list ({name, type, label?, …}
-- records); the result is the canonical {$record:{fields}} envelope the
-- type-system + FieldRenderer already consume.

module std where

@label "Record type"
@description "Build a `$record` FenelType value from a list of field-entry records: [FieldEntry] → {$record: {fields}}. The general runtime type-builder — constructs the `$`-key envelope dynamically (via assocRecord) since Fenel record literals can't carry a $-prefixed key."
@tags "type" "record" "reflection"
recordType : (fields: [{  }]) -> Type
recordType fields = assocRecord {} "$record" (assocRecord {} "fields" fields)
